 "notes": "Table XV Part II (Bilingualism), one mother tongue per opening; rows = the same 48 areas as Part I (Agency, four sub-agencies, states). Only Males and Females printed (persons null); no printed column numbers (cols null). subsidiary=null records are 'Number of persons speaking Mother Tongue'. Area names follow the Part I files (printed here 'Junagadh', 'Chunda', 'Malek Shri Joravar Khan's State (Varahi)' -> Part I 'Junagad', 'Chuda', \"Malek Shri Joravarkhan's State (Varahi)\"). Nil cells ('..', '....') omitted. Nawanagar Total subsidiary languages Males is clearly printed 607, but its subsidiary columns (Gujarati 507 + Western Hindi 69 + Balochi 71) sum to 647, and the Agency / Seventeen Salute States total 649 = 647 + Junagadh 2; so 607 looks like a misprint for 647. Kept as printed. Persian occupies a single page; leaf 473 (facing page) is only a 'Imperial Table XV, Part II—Bilingualism—contd.' divider with no figures."
}